LEGAL FRAMEWORK:
- Berne Convention for the Protection of Literary and Artistic Works
- Universal Declaration of Human Rights (UDHR)
- UNESCO Universal Copyright Convention
- UNICEF Child Rights Conventions (where applicable to accessible technology)
- Brazilian Federal Constitution Article 5 (Intellectual Property Rights)
- First Amendment and Fifth Amendment of the United States Constitution
- Automatic fines and "fractal state" enforcement mechanisms through
  international treaties and human rights agreements

This license represents a deeper commitment than standard corporate licenses,
embodying principles of:
- Ethical technology development
- Coherence with entropy and natural law
- Human rights-centered design
- Accessibility and universal access
- Transparency and interoperability

STANDARDS COMPLIANCE TARGETS:
This project is designed with the goal of adhering to the following standards,
and implementations strive to meet their requirements where applicable:

ISO Standards (Quality, Security, and Risk Management):
- ISO 9001 (Quality Management Systems)
- ISO 27001 (Information Security Management)
- ISO 27017 (Cloud Security Controls)
- ISO 27018 (Protection of PII in Public Clouds)
- ISO 8000 (Data Quality)
- ISO 25010 (Systems and Software Quality Models)
- ISO 27002, 22301, 31000 (Risk Management)

IEEE Standards (Software Engineering):
- IEEE 830 (Software Requirements Specifications)
- IEEE 1012 (Software Verification and Validation)
- IEEE 12207 (Software Life Cycle Processes)
- IEEE 14764 (Software Engineering — Software Life Cycle Processes — Maintenance)
- IEEE 1633 (Software Reliability)
- IEEE 42010 (Systems and Software Engineering — Architecture Description)
- IEEE 26514 (Software User Documentation)

NIST Frameworks (Security and Privacy):
- NIST Cybersecurity Framework (CSF)
- NIST SP 800-53 (Security and Privacy Controls)
- NIST SP 800-207 (Zero Trust Architecture)
- NIST AI Risk Management Framework

IETF RFCs (Internet Standards):
- RFC 5280 (Internet X.509 PKI Certificate and CRL Profile)
- RFC 7519 (JSON Web Token - JWT)
- RFC 7230 (HTTP/1.1 Message Syntax and Routing)
- RFC 8446 (TLS 1.3)
- RFC 8259 (JSON Data Interchange Format)
- Additional relevant RFCs as applicable

W3C Standards (Web Architecture):
- JSON specifications
- YAML specifications
- Web Architecture principles

ABNT/NBR (Brazilian Standards):
- Brazilian standards correlated with international standards

PRINCIPLE OF CONFLICT RESOLUTION:
In cases of conflict between standards or legal frameworks, the most protective
standard for human welfare and rights shall prevail.

IMPLEMENTATION COMMITMENT:
All code is written with these standards in mind, implementing their principles
where relevant to the project's functionality. Compliance is verified through:
- Code reviews against standards requirements
- Security analysis tools (CodeQL, static analyzers)
- Documentation of design decisions
- Testing for conformance with specifications

OPTIMIZATION GOALS:
- Efficiency and effectiveness
- Interoperability across versions
- Applicability and viability
- Mitigation strategies
- Adaptability and reliability
- Compatibility and stability
- Minimal footprint

